2) High level architecture
Monorepo

A monorepo means all apps and shared packages live in one Git repository.

Pros

Shared UI components and types

Easier consistency

One dev environment

Cons

Tooling needs discipline

Can become heavy if unmanaged

Recommended shape

apps/ contains runnable applications

packages/ contains shared code (UI, types, configs)

infra/ optional scripts for docker, db, ci

