7) How multi app navigation works locally

Each app runs on a different port:

Main: 3000

Payments: 3001

Service: 3002

Analytics: 3003

When you click a link in Main to open Payments:

it just navigates to http://localhost:3001

this is normal, they are separate web servers

Enterprise alternative:

Reverse proxy (Nginx) gives one domain and routes:

/payments -> payments app

/service -> service app

8) Light mode theme recommendation

For government, enterprise, and education style portals:

Light mode is common because it prints well, reads well, and feels formal.

Theme strategy:

Shared base theme (neutral background, consistent typography)

Unique accent per app:

Portal: blue

Payments: teal/green

Service: purple/indigo

Analytics: orange/amber

This creates recognition without looking like four separate brands.

9) Best practices you should follow
Data validation

Use Zod on the server for inputs.
Why:

prevents garbage data

reduces bugs

Error handling

Return consistent error payloads:

{ error: { code, message } }

Logging

In enterprise:

logs are structured JSON

include request id

Security basics

hash passwords (bcrypt)

protect routes with middleware

avoid storing secrets in git

use env vars

